<section class="custom-container grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-20 mt-32 mb-28">
  <div>
    <h2 class="heading-underline text-white font-display text-4xl max-w-[21ch] mb-6">
      The Challenge
    </h2>
    <div class="text-colorText-body max-w-[80ch] whitespace-pre-line">Campbellsville needed to promote their expanded online education offerings, so Wiley asked us to create spots that would relate to the challenges of returning to school in a busy world—with kids, jobs, and a whole life to live. Our goal was to shed a positive light on what it’s like to lead an already busy life and add school to the mix. We had to show Campbellsville as a path to something bigger and greater.</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2 class="heading-underline text-white font-display text-4xl max-w-[21ch] mb-6">
      Our Process
    </h2>
    <div class="text-colorText-body max-w-[80ch] whitespace-pre-line">Although Campbellsville University is based in Kentucky, we created video concepts centered around a student's home and work life that were shootable in Central Florida. With the Wiley team as a collaborative partner, we shot at three homes, two restaurants, and an office. Ultimately, we filmed and edited three unique ad spots to help students connect with the online back-to-school experience.</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2 class="heading-underline text-white font-display text-4xl max-w-[21ch] mb-6">
      The Results
    </h2>
    <div class="text-colorText-body max-w-[80ch] whitespace-pre-line">The new campaign for Campbellsville University was a success. The video spots we shot performed significantly higher than Campbellsville’s prior video assets and increased brand awareness and interest in the university’s online programs.

Today, we continue to help Wiley with projects for their college and university clients. </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="custom-container mb-28">
  <div class="bg-colorAccent-700 text-white text-center mx-auto py-16">
    <div class="max-w-[94ch] mx-auto">
      "Danny, Marshall, and the rest of Studio Say So run a class act operation. Their knowledge and experience were evident from concept to shooting to the final editing stages, and every effort was made to ensure we stayed true to the original vision. Above all, they engaged with us like true collaborators, listening and ensuring that we were all in sync every step of the way. Looking forward to an opportunity to work with them again!"
      <br />
      –Wiley
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
